And a fearsome clang about the temples the shining
helmet, being struck, kept up, and it was struck always
down along the well-made plates;

And always in grievous panting he was held, and down from him the sweat
from all sides out of his limbs, abundant, flowed, nor in any way was he able
to draw breath;

Hector, of Ajax the ashen spear, standing close by,
struck with his great sword by the socket of the point, behind,
and straight on cut it off;

And Ajax knew in his blameless heart, and shuddered at
the works of the gods, that entirely of battle the counsels cut short
Zeus the high-thundering, and wanted victory for the Trojans;

and in a pack they go from a dark-watered spring
to lap with slender tongues the dark water,
the top of it, belching up the gore of blood;

Such, the leaders and lords of the Myrmidons
about the good attendant of the fleet-footed descendant of Aeacus
were rushing;

And of the other rank Eudorus, warlike, was leader,
maiden’s son, whom bore, fair in the dance, Polymele,
daughter of Phylas;
